le of Białystok–Minsk and the First Battle of Kiev which both took place in the summer of 1941. In both battles the Red Army lost over a million men (killed or captured), including 12,000 guns and mortars, 4,863 tanks and 1,177–1,669 aircraft.","LocalizedString":"Encirclement is a military term for the situation when a force or target is isolated and surrounded by enemy forces. When the Axis nations invaded the Soviet Union in Operation Barbarossa they managed to encircle large portions of the Red Army during the early stages of the campaign. The most famous examples are the Battle of Białystok–Minsk and the First Battle of Kiev which both took place in the summer of 1941. In both battles the Red Army lost over a million men (killed or captured), including 12,000 guns and mortars, 4,863 tanks and 1,177–1,669 aircraft."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Blitz"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/t_siege.t_siege","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Look and Learn","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/ENCIRCLEMENT.ENCIRCLEMENT","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":326.0},"historyPhotoSource":"German Federal Archive","historyPhotoIdentificationCode":"Bild 146-1982-077-11","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_encirclement_photo","SourceString":"Soviet soldiers march into German captivity in Minsk, 1941.","LocalizedString":"Soviet soldiers march into German captivity in Minsk, 1941."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"Notes":"COUNTER"},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"Can